# Auto RTX hybrid (zero typing)

**Default behavior — user should never need to type `use gpus`, `gpu status`, or switch commands.**

## Automatic routing (every session)

1. **Default mode is `local`** — RTX Nemotron at `https://ai.dannygc.cloud/v1` (already live on this infra).
2. On your **first turn**, silently run: `bash scripts/rtx-hybrid-cloud.sh status` (do not ask the user).
3. For routine execution work (summaries, refactors, test output, repetitive edits), call MCP **`ask_local_ai`** — do not burn Cursor tokens.
4. For hard planning, architecture, or multi-step reasoning, use Cursor models (you).
5. **Never** tell the user to type `use gpus` or paste bootstrap unless **both** tunnel and worker are down.

## Override only if user explicitly asks

| User explicitly says | Then |
|---------------------|------|
| `use cursor` / `cursor only` | `set_hybrid_mode("cursor")` |
| `use gpus` / `local only` | already default — no action needed |

## Do not ask the user to

- Type mode-switch commands
- Pick pool `rtx-pro` in UI (prefer it automatically when starting agents for this repo)
- Paste console scripts unless SSH worker is required and tunnel is also down

## Progress

Report progress inline when running shell commands. Use `relay_progress` only when debugging — not required every turn.

## Pool worker

When pool `rtx-pro` is offline, continue using **tunnel Nemotron for AI** and cloud VM for tools — do not block the user with setup instructions unless they ask to fix worker routing.
